id: pm-web-957x
title: "pm-web test-add route passes a token shape the CLI rejects, so linking a test from the UI always fails"
description: "POST /api/projects/:projectId/pm/tests/:itemId builds ['test', id, '--add', '--command', command], but pm item test --add takes ONE CSV/JSON argument; the two-token --command form is rejected with exit 2, and --description is not a valid option on that path. The route now passes --add-json with the command and the optional description as the note key, which keeps commands containing commas or equals signs intact."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: bug,http-semantics,linked-tests
created_at: "2026-10-05T04:42:46.632Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T19:39:58.392Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T19:39:57.332Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T19:39:57.332Z"
author: pi-glm
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: HTTP linked-test mutation preserves a command containing commas and its optional note through an actual CLI read.
resolution: "Reverified main ca7e188bc91e (unchanged since audit): [PR #171](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/171) (139b75b) invalidates stale coverage reports, confines spawned PM_PATH, checks graph prerequisites before provisioning, and repairs close-many/test-add/plan positional and step-flag contracts with real integration regressions. Retained evidence: scripts/coverage-gate.ts, src/routes/pm.ts, src/services/pm-runner.ts."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T05:08:29.695Z",codex-sol,"Resumed regression suite passes against real HTTP, disposable PostgreSQL, and a scratch pm project (4/4). Preserved the interrupted implementation. Linked-test JSON also needed a single-entry array at the SDK dispatch boundary. Explicit persisted-record and bulk membership assertions pin the behavior."
